[["Map",1,2,5044,5045],"docs",["Map",3,4,18,19,30,31,42,43,54,55,66,67,78,79,114,115,154,155,200,201,232,233,297,298,340,341,381,382,444,445,409,487,539,540,597,598,222,648,684,685,718,719,798,799,832,833,970,971,1014,1015,1124,1125,1154,1155,1231,1232,1276,1277,1391,1392,1424,1425,1504,1505,1636,1637,1666,1667,1805,1806,1914,1915,1950,1951,2069,2070,2200,2201,2255,2256,2343,2344,2388,2389,2421,2422,2524,2525,2590,2591,2620,2621,2733,2734,2784,2785,271,2817,2845,2846,2856,2857,2885,2886,2931,2932,2960,2961,2996,2997,3030,3031,3061,3062,3094,3095,665,3129,3191,3192,3202,3203,3260,3261,3329,3330,3374,3375,3425,3426,3482,3483,3539,3540,3612,3613,3655,3656,3695,3696,3739,3740,3777,3778,3837,3838,3886,3887,3972,3973,4034,4035,4081,4082,4158,4159,4202,4203,4249,4250,480,4289,4372,4373,4457,4458,4667,4668,4863,4864],"agents",{"id":3,"data":5,"body":15,"filePath":16,"digest":17,"deferredRender":8},{"title":6,"description":7,"editUrl":8,"head":9,"template":10,"sidebar":11,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Agents Overview","Learn about FunctionFly Agents - autonomous AI entities with memory, behavioral policies, and enterprise-grade security.",true,[],"doc",{"order":12,"hidden":13,"attrs":14},1,false,{},"import { Card, CardGrid } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';\n\nFunctionFly Agents are autonomous AI entities that can execute tasks, make decisions, and evolve over time based on their behavioral policies. Built for production with enterprise-grade security.\n\n## Key Features\n\n\u003CCardGrid>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Autonomous Execution\" icon=\"seti:custom\">\n    Agents can execute tasks autonomously based on configured behavioral policies without requiring approval for each action.\n  \u003C/Card>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Memory & Context\" icon=\"seti:memory\">\n    Multiple memory types (short-term, long-term, episodic, semantic) enable agents to maintain context across interactions.\n  \u003C/Card>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Behavioral Policies\" icon=\"seti:lock\">\n    Safety limits and operational boundaries ensure agents operate within defined parameters.\n  \u003C/Card>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Enterprise Security\" icon=\"shield\">\n    Zero-knowledge encryption, API key management, and compliance-ready audit logging built in.\n  \u003C/Card>\n\u003C/CardGrid>\n\n## Agent Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        Agent                                │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────────────┐  │\n│  │   Memory    │  │  Policy     │  │     Capabilities    │  │\n│  │   System    │  │  Engine     │  │                     │  │\n│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────────────┘  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                      SDK Interface                          │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                      REST API                               │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Agent States\n\n| State | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `initializing` | Agent is being set up |\n| `idle` | Agent is ready but not executing |\n| `busy` | Agent is processing a task |\n| `error` | Agent encountered an error |\n| `stopped` | Agent has been manually stopped |\n\n## Production Readiness Checklist\n\nBefore deploying agents to production, ensure:\n\n- [ ] **API Key Security** - Each agent has a dedicated API key with minimal required permissions\n- [ ] **Behavioral Policies** - Max execution depth, recursion limits, and timeouts configured\n- [ ] **Memory Encryption** - Sensitive data in memory is encrypted at rest\n- [ ] **Monitoring** - Alerts configured for policy violations and unusual activity\n- [ ] **Cost Controls** - Wallet limits and spending alerts configured\n- [ ] **Audit Logging** - Agent actions are logged for compliance\n\n## Quick Links\n\n- [Create Your First Agent](/guides/creating-agents/) - Step-by-step guide\n- [Agent Marketplace](/agents/marketplace/) - Discover pre-built agents\n- [SDK Integration](/agents/sdk/) - Programmatic access\n- [Agent Security](/agents/security/) - Production security best practices\n- [Behavioral Policies](/agents/policies/) - Configure safety limits\n- [Agent Memory](/agents/memory/) - Understand memory types","src/content/docs/agents/index.mdx","710887c67ce4274b","agents/marketplace",{"id":18,"data":20,"body":27,"filePath":28,"digest":29,"deferredRender":8},{"title":21,"description":22,"editUrl":8,"head":23,"template":10,"sidebar":24,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Agent Marketplace","Discover, install, and manage pre-built agents from the FunctionFly marketplace.",[],{"order":25,"hidden":13,"attrs":26},2,{},"The Agent Marketplace provides pre-built agents that you can install and customize for your use case.\n\n## Browse Agents\n\nVisit the [Agent Marketplace](/agents/marketplace/) in your dashboard or browse via API:\n\n```bash\n# List available agents\ncurl https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n### Filtering Agents\n\n```bash\n# Filter by category\ncurl \"https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents?category=productivity\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n\n# Filter by capabilities\ncurl \"https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents?capabilities=web_search,code_execution\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n\n# Search by description\ncurl \"https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents?search=image+processing\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n## Agent Categories\n\n| Category | Description | Examples |\n|----------|-------------|----------|\n| `productivity` | Task automation | Scheduler, reminders, organizer |\n| `development` | Coding assistance | Code reviewer, debugger, docs writer |\n| `research` | Data analysis | Researcher, data analyzer, fact checker |\n| `communication` | Messaging | Email assistant, summarizer, translator |\n| `security` | Monitoring | Threat detector, anomaly detector |\n| `custom` | User-created | Community agents |\n\n## Installing an Agent\n\n### From Dashboard\n\n1. Navigate to **Agent Marketplace**\n2. Find the agent you want\n3. Click **Install**\n4. Configure initial settings\n5. Click **Deploy**\n\n### Via API\n\n```bash\n# Install an agent from marketplace\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents/INSTALL_ID/install \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"name\": \"my-research-agent\",\n    \"configuration\": {\n      \"max_execution_depth\": 3,\n      \"allowed_tools\": [\"web_search\", \"code_execution\"]\n    }\n  }'\n```\n\n## Agent Templates\n\n### Code Reviewer Agent\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents/code-reviewer/install \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"name\": \"my-code-reviewer\",\n    \"configuration\": {\n      \"languages\": [\"python\", \"javascript\", \"go\"],\n      \"review_depth\": \"detailed\",\n      \"auto_fix\": false\n    }\n  }'\n```\n\n### Data Analyzer Agent\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents/data-analyzer/install \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"name\": \"my-analyzer\",\n    \"configuration\": {\n      \"data_sources\": [\"csv\", \"api\"],\n      \"visualization\": true,\n      \"export_formats\": [\"json\", \"csv\", \"pdf\"]\n    }\n  }'\n```\n\n## Publishing Your Agent\n\n### Prepare Your Agent\n\n```javascript\n// manifest.json - Agent metadata\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-custom-agent\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"description\": \"A helpful assistant for...\",\n  \"category\": \"productivity\",\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"web_search\": true,\n    \"code_execution\": true\n  },\n  \"behavioral_policy\": {\n    \"max_execution_depth\": 3,\n    \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 60\n  },\n  \"inputs\": [\n    { \"name\": \"query\", \"type\": \"string\", \"required\": true }\n  ],\n  \"outputs\": [\n    { \"name\": \"result\", \"type\": \"string\" }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Test Your Agent\n\n```bash\n# Test before publishing\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/TEST_AGENT_ID/test \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"task\": \"Your test task here\",\n    \"expected_output\": \"Expected behavior\"\n  }'\n```\n\n### Publish to Marketplace\n\n```bash\n# Submit for review\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/submit \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"agent_id\": \"your-agent-id\",\n    \"manifest\": { ... },\n    \"documentation\": \"Agent usage docs...\",\n    \"support_contact\": \"support@yourcompany.com\"\n  }'\n```\n\n### Review Process\n\n1. **Automated Testing** - Runs test cases against your agent\n2. **Security Scan** - Checks for vulnerabilities\n3. **Manual Review** - Marketplace team reviews\n4. **Approval** - Agent published to marketplace\n\n## Managing Installed Agents\n\n### List Installed Agents\n\n```bash\ncurl https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n### Update Agent\n\n```bash\n# Update agent configuration\ncurl -X PATCH https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/YOUR_AGENT_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"configuration\": {\n      \"max_execution_depth\": 5,\n      \"allowed_tools\": [\"web_search\"]\n    }\n  }'\n```\n\n### Uninstall Agent\n\n```bash\ncurl -X DELETE https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/YOUR_AGENT_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n## Marketplace Analytics\n\n### Agent Performance\n\nView performance metrics for your installed agents:\n\n| Metric | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| `executions` | Total task executions |\n| `success_rate` | Percentage of successful tasks |\n| `avg_duration` | Average execution time |\n| `cost` | Total compute cost |\n| `rating` | User rating (1-5 stars) |\n\n### Agent Versioning\n\n```bash\n# List agent versions\ncurl https://api.functionfly.com/v1/marketplace/agents/AGENT_ID/versions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n\n# Pin to specific version\ncurl -X PATCH https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/YOUR_AGENT_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{ \"version\": \"1.2.0\" }'\n\n# Enable auto-update\ncurl -X PATCH https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/YOUR_AGENT_ID \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '{ \"auto_update\": true, \"update_channel\": \"stable\" }'\n```","src/content/docs/agents/marketplace.mdx","080e7560ec674026","agents/memory",{"id":30,"data":32,"body":39,"filePath":40,"digest":41,"deferredRender":8},{"title":33,"description":34,"editUrl":8,"head":35,"template":10,"sidebar":36,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Agent Memory","Understand how FunctionFly Agents use different memory types to maintain context and learn over time.",[],{"order":37,"hidden":13,"attrs":38},6,{},"FunctionFly Agents use a sophisticated memory system to maintain context across interactions, learn from experiences, and provide personalized responses.\n\n## Memory Architecture\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                      Agent Memory                           │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌─────────────┐  ┌────┐  │\n│  │ Short-Term  │  │  Long-Term  │  │  Episodic   │  │Se- │  │\n│  │   Memory    │  │   Memory    │  │   Memory    │  │man-│  │\n│  │             │  │             │  │             │  │tic │  │\n│  │  Session    │  │  Persistent │  │   Event     │  │ tic│  │\n│  │  Context    │  │  User Data  │  │  History    │  │    │  │\n│  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └─────────────┘  └────┘  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    Memory Manager                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    Vector Store                              │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n## Memory Types\n\n### Short-Term Memory\n\nUsed for current session context. Fast access, limited capacity.\n\n```javascript\n// Store in short-term memory\nawait agent.memory.shortTerm.store('current_task', {\n  goal: 'Research AI developments',\n  progress: 'completed web search',\n  next_step: 'analyze findings'\n});\n\n// Retrieve\nconst context = await agent.memory.shortTerm.get('current_task');\n```\n\n**Use cases:**\n- Active task state\n- Conversation context\n- Temporary calculations\n\n### Long-Term Memory\n\nPersistent storage for user preferences and learned information.\n\n```javascript\n// Store in long-term memory\nawait agent.memory.longTerm.store('user_preferences', {\n  theme: 'dark',\n  language: 'en',\n  communication_style: 'concise'\n});\n\n// Search long-term memory\nconst preferences = await agent.memory.longTerm.search('theme preference');\n```\n\n**Use cases:**\n- User preferences\n- Historical interactions\n- Learned patterns\n\n### Episodic Memory\n\nStores specific events and experiences for later recall.\n\n```javascript\n// Record an experience\nawait agent.memory.episodic.record({\n  timestamp: Date.now(),\n  event: 'user_asked_about_pricing',\n  context: 'User was evaluating enterprise plan',\n  outcome: 'Provided pricing breakdown',\n  tags: ['pricing', 'enterprise', 'evaluation']\n});\n\n// Recall similar experiences\nconst similar = await agent.memory.episodic.recall({\n  tags: ['pricing', 'enterprise']\n});\n```\n\n**Use cases:**\n- Event history\n- Success/failure patterns\n- Decision rationale\n\n### Semantic Memory\n\nStores learned knowledge and facts. Uses vector embeddings for semantic search.\n\n```javascript\n// Store learned knowledge\nawait agent.memory.semantic.store('product_knowledge', {\n  fact: 'FunctionFly supports Python, JavaScript, Go, and Rust',\n  source: 'product documentation',\n  confidence: 0.95,\n  expires_at: null\n});\n\n// Semantic search\nconst relevant = await agent.memory.semantic.search(\n  'What languages does FunctionFly support?'\n);\n```\n\n**Use cases:**\n- Factual knowledge\n- Learned concepts\n- Semantic relationships\n\n## Vector Store\n\nAgent memory uses vector embeddings for similarity search:\n\n```javascript\n// Configure vector store\nagent.memory.configure({\n  vectorStore: {\n    provider: 'pgvector',\n    dimensions: 1536,\n    metric: 'cosine'\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Supported Providers\n\n| Provider | Description | Best For |\n|----------|-------------|----------|\n| `pgvector` | PostgreSQL extension | Self-hosted |\n| `pinecone` | Managed vector DB | Production |\n| `weaviate` | Open source vector | Hybrid |\n| `memory` | Built-in (default) | Development |\n\n## Memory Operations\n\n### Store Data\n\n```javascript\n// Generic store (auto-selects memory type)\nawait agent.memory.store('key', { data: 'value' });\n\n// Explicit type selection\nawait agent.memory.store('key', data, { type: 'long_term' });\n```\n\n### Retrieve Data\n\n```javascript\n// Get with fallback\nconst data = await agent.memory.get('key', {\n  default: 'fallback_value',\n  type: 'short_term'\n});\n```\n\n### Search\n\n```javascript\n// Semantic search across all memory\nconst results = await agent.memory.search('query', {\n  limit: 10,\n  threshold: 0.8\n});\n\n// Type-specific search\nconst results = await agent.memory.search('query', {\n  type: 'semantic',\n  limit: 5\n});\n```\n\n### Delete\n\n```javascript\n// Delete specific key\nawait agent.memory.delete('key');\n\n// Clear by type\nawait agent.memory.clear('short_term');\n\n// Clear all\nawait agent.memory.clear('all');\n```\n\n## Memory Configuration\n\n### Encryption\n\nEncrypt sensitive memory:\n\n```javascript\nagent.memory.configure({\n  encryption: {\n    enabled: true,\n    key: process.env.MEMORY_ENCRYPTION_KEY,\n    algorithm: 'AES-256-GCM'\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Retention Policies\n\n```javascript\nagent.memory.configure({\n  retention: {\n    short_term: { max_age_days: 1 },\n    long_term: { max_age_days: 365 },\n    episodic: { max_events: 10000 },\n    semantic: { max_entries: 50000 }\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Automatic Cleanup\n\n```javascript\nagent.memory.configure({\n  auto_cleanup: {\n    enabled: true,\n    schedule: 'daily',\n    preserve_important: true\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Memory in Production\n\n### Performance Optimization\n\n```javascript\n// Use caching for frequent reads\nagent.memory.configure({\n  cache: {\n    enabled: true,\n    max_size_mb: 128,\n    ttl_seconds: 300\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Monitoring\n\n```javascript\n// Monitor memory usage\nagent.memory.on('usage_alert', (alert) => {\n  if (alert.type === 'memory_full') {\n    // Trigger cleanup\n    await agent.memory.cleanup();\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Backup\n\n```javascript\n// Export memory state\nconst backup = await agent.memory.export({\n  format: 'json',\n  include_vectors: false\n});\n\n// Import backup\nawait agent.memory.import(backup);\n```\n\n## Security Considerations\n\n### Sensitive Data Handling\n\n```javascript\n// Mark sensitive data\nawait agent.memory.store('api_key', sensitiveData, {\n  encrypted: true,\n  access_audit: true\n});\n\n// Access with verification\nconst data = await agent.memory.get('api_key', {\n  verify_access: true,\n  reason: 'needed for external call'\n});\n```\n\n### Access Control\n\n```javascript\nagent.memory.configure({\n  access_control: {\n    require_auth: true,\n    allowed_roles: ['agent', 'admin'],\n    audit_reads: true,\n    audit_writes: true\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Memory Not Persisting\n\n1. Check retention policy settings\n2. Verify vector store connection\n3. Check disk space\n\n### Slow Retrieval\n\n1. Enable caching\n2. Reduce vector dimensions\n3. Optimize search queries\n\n### Memory Full\n\n1. Trigger manual cleanup\n2. Increase retention policy strictness\n3. Archive old episodic memories","src/content/docs/agents/memory.mdx","b83bf4f65284d994","agents/policies",{"id":42,"data":44,"body":51,"filePath":52,"digest":53,"deferredRender":8},{"title":45,"description":46,"editUrl":8,"head":47,"template":10,"sidebar":48,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Behavioral Policies","Configure safety limits and operational boundaries for FunctionFly Agents.",[],{"order":49,"hidden":13,"attrs":50},5,{},"Behavioral policies define how your agent operates, including safety limits, tool access, and operational boundaries.\n\n## Policy Structure\n\n```json\n{\n  \"behavioral_policy\": {\n    \"max_execution_depth\": 5,\n    \"max_recursion_depth\": 3,\n    \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 300,\n    \"max_memory_mb\": 512,\n    \"max_cost_per_execution\": 1.00,\n    \"allowed_tools\": [\"web_search\", \"code_execution\"],\n    \"blocked_tools\": [],\n    \"blocked_topics\": [],\n    \"require_approval_for\": [],\n    \"rate_limit\": {\n      \"requests_per_minute\": 60,\n      \"concurrent_executions\": 5\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Core Parameters\n\n### Execution Limits\n\n| Parameter | Default | Min | Max | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-----|-----|-------------|\n| `max_execution_depth` | 5 | 1 | 10 | Nested tool calls |\n| `max_recursion_depth` | 3 | 1 | 5 | Recursive operations |\n| `max_wall_time_seconds` | 300 | 5 | 3600 | Execution timeout |\n| `max_memory_mb` | 512 | 64 | 4096 | Memory limit |\n\n### Cost Controls\n\n| Parameter | Default | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| `max_cost_per_execution` | 1.00 | Max spend per task (USD) |\n| `daily_spend_limit` | 100.00 | Daily budget cap |\n\n## Tool Control\n\n### Allowed Tools\n\nDefine which tools the agent can use:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"allowed_tools\": [\n    \"web_search\",\n    \"code_execution\",\n    \"file_read\",\n    \"api_calls\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Available Tools\n\n| Tool | Description | Security Risk |\n|------|-------------|---------------|\n| `web_search` | Search the web | Low |\n| `code_execution` | Run code in sandbox | Medium |\n| `file_read` | Read files | Medium |\n| `file_write` | Write files | High |\n| `api_calls` | External API requests | Medium |\n| `database_queries` | Query databases | High |\n| `shell_commands` | Execute shell commands | Critical |\n\n### Blocking Dangerous Tools\n\n```json\n{\n  \"blocked_tools\": [\n    \"shell_commands\",\n    \"database_queries\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Topic Restrictions\n\nPrevent agents from engaging with sensitive topics:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"blocked_topics\": [\n    \"financial_advice\",\n    \"medical_diagnosis\",\n    \"legal_counsel\",\n    \"harmful_content\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Topic Blocking\n\n```json\n{\n  \"blocked_topics\": [\n    \"political_content\",\n    \"religious_debate\",\n    \"competitor_analysis\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_topics_regex\": [\n    \"^secret_\",\n    \"^confidential_\",\n    \"^do_not_share\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## Approval Requirements\n\nRequire human approval for sensitive actions:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"require_approval_for\": [\n    \"file_deletion\",\n    \"external_api_calls\",\n    \"database_writes\",\n    \"large_data_access\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Approval Workflow\n\n```javascript\nagent.on('approval_required', async (event) => {\n  const { action, details, callbackUrl } = event;\n\n  // Send to approval queue\n  const approval = await sendForApproval({\n    agentId: agent.id,\n    action,\n    details,\n    callbackUrl\n  });\n\n  // Wait for approval\n  if (approval.status === 'approved') {\n    return { proceed: true };\n  } else {\n    return { proceed: false, reason: approval.reason };\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Rate Limiting\n\nControl agent request rates:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"rate_limit\": {\n    \"requests_per_minute\": 60,\n    \"requests_per_hour\": 1000,\n    \"concurrent_executions\": 5,\n    \"burst_allowance\": 10\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Policy Templates\n\n### Development\n\n```json\n{\n  \"max_execution_depth\": 10,\n  \"max_recursion_depth\": 5,\n  \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 600,\n  \"max_memory_mb\": 1024,\n  \"allowed_tools\": [\"web_search\", \"code_execution\", \"file_read\", \"file_write\"]\n}\n```\n\n### Production (Restrictive)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"max_execution_depth\": 3,\n  \"max_recursion_depth\": 2,\n  \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 60,\n  \"max_memory_mb\": 256,\n  \"max_cost_per_execution\": 0.50,\n  \"allowed_tools\": [\"web_search\"],\n  \"blocked_topics\": [\"financial_advice\", \"medical_diagnosis\", \"legal_counsel\"],\n  \"require_approval_for\": [\"file_deletion\", \"api_calls\"]\n}\n```\n\n### High-Security\n\n```json\n{\n  \"max_execution_depth\": 2,\n  \"max_recursion_depth\": 1,\n  \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 30,\n  \"max_memory_mb\": 128,\n  \"max_cost_per_execution\": 0.25,\n  \"allowed_tools\": [],\n  \"blocked_topics\": [\"*\"],\n  \"require_approval_for\": [\"*\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Updating Policies\n\n### Runtime Updates\n\n```javascript\n// Update policy at runtime\nawait agent.updatePolicy({\n  max_wall_time_seconds: 60,\n  allowed_tools: [\"web_search\", \"code_execution\"]\n});\n```\n\n### Versioned Policies\n\n```javascript\n// Create new policy version\nconst newPolicy = await agent.policies.create({\n  name: \"v2-restrictive\",\n  rules: { ... },\n  rollout_percentage: 10 // A/B testing\n});\n```\n\n## Policy Violation Handling\n\n### Violation Types\n\n| Type | Severity | Action |\n|------|----------|--------|\n| `execution_limit` | Medium | Stop execution |\n| `tool_access` | High | Block and alert |\n| `topic_restriction` | Medium | Redirect |\n| `rate_limit` | Low | Queue request |\n\n### Custom Violation Handlers\n\n```javascript\nagent.on('policy_violation', (event) => {\n  const { type, details, policy } = event;\n\n  if (type === 'execution_limit') {\n    // Log and continue with reduced limits\n    agent.reduceLimits();\n  } else if (type === 'tool_access') {\n    // Block and alert security team\n    await securityAlert({ event });\n    return { blocked: true };\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Monitoring Policy Effectiveness\n\n### Metrics to Track\n\n- Policy violations per agent\n- Average execution depth used\n- Tool usage patterns\n- Rate limit hits\n- Approval request frequency\n\n### Dashboard Metrics\n\n| Metric | Target | Alert Threshold |\n|--------|--------|-----------------|\n| Violations/day | \u003C 5 | > 20 |\n| Avg execution depth | \u003C 50% of max | > 80% |\n| Tool usage diversity | Stable | Sudden changes |\n| Approval queue depth | \u003C 10 | > 50 |","src/content/docs/agents/policies.mdx","b594e030acdde350","agents/sdk",{"id":54,"data":56,"body":63,"filePath":64,"digest":65,"deferredRender":8},{"title":57,"description":58,"editUrl":8,"head":59,"template":10,"sidebar":60,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Agent SDK Integration","Programmatic access to FunctionFly Agents via SDK for Node.js, Python, Go, and more.",[],{"order":61,"hidden":13,"attrs":62},3,{},"Integrate FunctionFly Agents into your applications using our multi-language SDKs.\n\n## Available SDKs\n\n| SDK | Package | Documentation |\n|-----|---------|---------------|\n| Node.js | `@functionfly/agent-sdk` | [Guide](/sdks/javascript/) |\n| Python | `functionfly-agent` | [Guide](/sdks/python/) |\n| Go | `github.com/functionfly/agent-go` | [Guide](/sdks/go/) |\n| Rust | `functionfly-agent` | [Guide](/sdks/rust/) |\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\n# Node.js\nnpm install @functionfly/agent-sdk\n\n# Python\npip install functionfly-agent\n\n# Go\ngo get github.com/functionfly/agent-go\n\n# Rust\ncargo add functionfly-agent\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### Node.js\n\n```javascript\nimport { FunctionFlyAgent } from '@functionfly/agent-sdk';\n\n// Initialize agent\nconst agent = new FunctionFlyAgent({\n  agentId: process.env.FFLY_AGENT_ID,\n  apiKey: process.env.FFLY_AGENT_API_KEY\n});\n\n// Execute a task\nconst result = await agent.execute({\n  task: 'Research the latest developments in AI',\n  context: { depth: 'comprehensive' }\n});\n\nconsole.log(result);\n```\n\n### Python\n\n```python\nfrom functionfly_agent import FunctionFlyAgent\n\n# Initialize agent\nagent = FunctionFlyAgent(\n    agent_id=os.environ[\"FFLY_AGENT_ID\"],\n    api_key=os.environ[\"FFLY_AGENT_API_KEY\"]\n)\n\n# Execute a task\nresult = agent.execute(\n    task=\"Research the latest developments in AI\",\n    context={\"depth\": \"comprehensive\"}\n)\n\nprint(result)\n```\n\n### Go\n\n```go\nimport \"github.com/functionfly/agent-go\"\n\nagent := functionfly.NewAgent(functionfly.Config{\n    AgentID: os.Getenv(\"FFLY_AGENT_ID\"),\n    APIKey:  os.Getenv(\"FFLY_AGENT_API_KEY\"),\n})\n\nresult, err := agent.Execute(context.Background(), &functionfly.ExecuteRequest{\n    Task:    \"Research the latest developments in AI\",\n    Context: map[string]interface{}{\"depth\": \"comprehensive\"},\n})\n```\n\n## Configuration Options\n\n### Basic Configuration\n\n```javascript\nconst agent = new FunctionFlyAgent({\n  agentId: 'your-agent-id',\n  apiKey: process.env.FFLY_AGENT_API_KEY,\n\n  // Optional configuration\n  timeout: 30000,           // Request timeout in ms\n  retries: 3,               // Retry on failure\n  region: 'us-east-1',       // Specify region\n  version: 'stable',        // Agent version\n});\n```\n\n### Advanced Configuration\n\n```javascript\nconst agent = new FunctionFlyAgent({\n  agentId: 'your-agent-id',\n  apiKey: process.env.FFLY_AGENT_API_KEY,\n\n  // Retry configuration\n  retry: {\n    maxAttempts: 3,\n    backoff: 'exponential',\n    initialDelay: 1000,\n    maxDelay: 30000,\n  },\n\n  // Circuit breaker\n  circuitBreaker: {\n    enabled: true,\n    threshold: 5,           // Failures before opening\n    timeout: 60000,         // Time to wait before half-open\n  },\n\n  // Caching\n  cache: {\n    enabled: true,\n    ttl: 300,               // Cache TTL in seconds\n    maxSize: 100,           // Max cached items\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Agent Operations\n\n### Execute Task\n\n```javascript\n// Simple execution\nconst result = await agent.execute({\n  task: 'Analyze this data and provide insights',\n  data: { /* your data */ }\n});\n\n// With options\nconst result = await agent.execute({\n  task: 'Analyze this data',\n  data: { /* your data */ },\n  options: {\n    waitForCompletion: true,  // Wait for result (vs. async)\n    timeout: 60000,          // Max wait time\n    correlationId: 'req-123', // For tracking\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Async Execution\n\n```javascript\n// Start execution without waiting\nconst handle = await agent.executeAsync({\n  task: 'Process large dataset',\n  data: { /* large data */ }\n});\n\n// Poll for result\nconst result = await handle.wait({ timeout: 300000 });\n\n// Or check status\nconst status = await handle.status();\n```\n\n### Streaming Responses\n\n```javascript\n// Stream response as it's generated\nconst stream = await agent.executeStream({\n  task: 'Write a detailed report on...'\n});\n\nfor await (const chunk of stream) {\n  console.log(chunk);\n}\n```\n\n## Memory Operations\n\n### Store in Memory\n\n```javascript\n// Store context for later use\nawait agent.memory.store('user_context', {\n  preferences: { theme: 'dark' },\n  history: ['action1', 'action2']\n});\n\n// Store with expiration\nawait agent.memory.store('temp_data', data, {\n  ttl: 3600  // 1 hour\n});\n```\n\n### Retrieve from Memory\n\n```javascript\n// Get specific data\nconst context = await agent.memory.get('user_context');\n\n// Search memory\nconst results = await agent.memory.search('user preferences');\n```\n\n## Policy Management\n\n### Get Current Policy\n\n```javascript\nconst policy = await agent.getPolicy();\nconsole.log(policy);\n```\n\n### Update Policy\n\n```javascript\nawait agent.updatePolicy({\n  max_execution_depth: 3,\n  max_wall_time_seconds: 60,\n  allowed_tools: ['web_search', 'code_execution']\n});\n```\n\n### Policy Events\n\n```javascript\n// Listen for policy violations\nagent.on('policy_violation', (event) => {\n  console.log('Policy violated:', event.details);\n});\n\n// Listen for approval requests\nagent.on('approval_required', async (event) => {\n  const action = await getHumanApproval(event);\n  return action;\n});\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Error Types\n\n```javascript\ntry {\n  const result = await agent.execute({ task: '...' });\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof AgentTimeoutError) {\n    // Execution took too long\n  } else if (error instanceof AgentPolicyViolationError) {\n    // Action blocked by policy\n  } else if (error instanceof AgentAuthError) {\n    // Authentication failed\n  } else if (error instanceof AgentRateLimitError) {\n    // Too many requests\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Retry Logic\n\n```javascript\nconst agent = new FunctionFlyAgent({\n  // ... config\n  retry: {\n    maxAttempts: 3,\n    on: [AgentTimeoutError, AgentRateLimitError],\n    backoff: 'exponential'\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Webhooks\n\n### Register Webhook\n\n```javascript\nagent.webhooks.register({\n  url: 'https://your-server.com/webhook',\n  events: ['execution_complete', 'policy_violation', 'error'],\n  secret: process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET\n});\n```\n\n### Verify Webhook Signature\n\n```javascript\nfunction verifyWebhook(signature, payload, secret) {\n  const expected = crypto\n    .createHmac('sha256', secret)\n    .update(payload)\n    .digest('hex');\n  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(\n    Buffer.from(signature),\n    Buffer.from(expected)\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## TypeScript Support\n\n```typescript\nimport { FunctionFlyAgent, type ExecuteOptions, type AgentConfig } from '@functionfly/agent-sdk';\n\n// Full type safety\nconst config: AgentConfig = {\n  agentId: process.env.FLLY_AGENT_ID!,\n  apiKey: process.env.FLLY_AGENT_API_KEY!,\n  timeout: 30000,\n};\n\nconst agent = new FunctionFlyAgent(config);\n\nconst options: ExecuteOptions = {\n  waitForCompletion: true,\n  timeout: 60000,\n};\n\nconst result = await agent.execute({\n  task: 'Analyze the data',\n  options\n});\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use Environment Variables** - Never hardcode API keys\n2. **Implement Retry Logic** - Handle transient failures\n3. **Set Timeouts** - Prevent hanging requests\n4. **Monitor Usage** - Track costs and performance\n5. **Handle Errors Gracefully** - Provide fallbacks\n6. **Use Streaming** - For long-running tasks\n7. **Secure Webhooks** - Always verify signatures","src/content/docs/agents/sdk.mdx","89f5fec4755f40fc","agents/security",{"id":66,"data":68,"body":75,"filePath":76,"digest":77,"deferredRender":8},{"title":69,"description":70,"editUrl":8,"head":71,"template":10,"sidebar":72,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Agent Security","Production security best practices for FunctionFly Agents including API key management, encryption, and compliance.",[],{"order":73,"hidden":13,"attrs":74},4,{},"Security is critical when deploying autonomous agents. This guide covers production-ready security configurations.\n\n## API Key Management\n\n### Per-Agent Keys\n\nEach agent should have its own API key with minimal permissions:\n\n```bash\n# Create agent-specific API key\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/YOUR_AGENT_ID/keys \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"name\": \"production-agent-key\",\n    \"permissions\": [\"execute\", \"memory:read\", \"memory:write\"],\n    \"expires_at\": \"2025-12-31T23:59:59Z\"\n  }'\n```\n\n### Key Rotation\n\nRotate agent keys regularly:\n\n```bash\n# Rotate agent key\ncurl -X POST https://api.functionfly.com/v1/agents/YOUR_AGENT_ID/keys/rotate \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY\"\n```\n\n### Never Commit Keys\n\nStore agent API keys in environment variables, never in code:\n\n```bash\n# Environment variable (correct)\nexport FFLY_AGENT_API_KEY=\"sk_agent_...\"\n\n# ❌ Never do this\n# const agentKey = \"sk_agent_...\"; // Hardcoded!\n```\n\n## Zero-Knowledge Memory Encryption\n\nAgent memory is encrypted by default. For enhanced security:\n\n```javascript\n// Enable additional encryption for sensitive memory\nawait agent.memory.configure({\n  encryptionEnabled: true,\n  encryptionKey: process.env.MEMORY_ENCRYPTION_KEY\n});\n```\n\n### Memory Security Levels\n\n| Level | Description | Use Case |\n|-------|-------------|----------|\n| `standard` | Default encryption | General purpose |\n| `enhanced` | Additional encryption layer | Sensitive data |\n| `isolated` | Memory isolated per session | High-security operations |\n\n## Behavioral Policy Security\n\nConfigure strict policies to prevent unintended actions:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"behavioral_policy\": {\n    \"max_execution_depth\": 3,\n    \"max_recursion_depth\": 2,\n    \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 60,\n    \"max_memory_mb\": 256,\n    \"allowed_tools\": [\"web_search\", \"code_execution\"],\n    \"blocked_topics\": [\"financial_advice\", \"medical_diagnosis\"],\n    \"require_approval_for\": [\"file_deletion\", \"api_calls_external\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Security-First Policy Defaults\n\n```json\n{\n  \"max_execution_depth\": 2,\n  \"max_recursion_depth\": 1,\n  \"max_wall_time_seconds\": 30,\n  \"max_memory_mb\": 128,\n  \"allowed_tools\": [],\n  \"blocked_topics\": [\"*\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Audit Logging\n\nEnable comprehensive audit logging for compliance:\n\n```javascript\n// Configure audit logging\nagent.configure({\n  auditLogging: {\n    enabled: true,\n    level: \"verbose\",\n    retentionDays: 90,\n    events: [\n      \"execution_start\",\n      \"execution_complete\",\n      \"policy_violation\",\n      \"memory_access\",\n      \"tool_usage\"\n    ]\n  }\n});\n```\n\n### Audit Event Types\n\n| Event | Description |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `execution_start` | Agent begins processing |\n| `execution_complete` | Task finished successfully |\n| `execution_error` | Task failed |\n| `policy_violation` | Action blocked by policy |\n| `memory_access` | Read/write to agent memory |\n| `tool_usage` | External tool invocation |\n| `approval_request` | Human approval requested |\n\n## Network Security\n\n### Outbound Connections\n\nControl what agents can access:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"network_policy\": {\n    \"allowed_domains\": [\"api.stripe.com\", \"your-service.com\"],\n    \"blocked_domains\": [\"malicious-site.com\", \"庞统.cn\"],\n    \"max_requests_per_minute\": 100\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Webhook Security\n\nSecure webhook endpoints for agent callbacks:\n\n```javascript\n// Verify webhook signatures\nfunction verifyWebhookSignature(payload, signature, secret) {\n  const expected = crypto\n    .createHmac('sha256', secret)\n    .update(payload)\n    .digest('hex');\n  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(\n    Buffer.from(signature),\n    Buffer.from(expected)\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Compliance Considerations\n\n### Data Residency\n\nConfigure agent data residency:\n\n```bash\n# Set data residency for agent operations\nexport FFLY_AGENT_DATA_REGION=\"us-east-1\"\n```\n\n### GDPR Compliance\n\nFor agents processing EU data:\n\n```javascript\nagent.configure({\n  gdprCompliant: true,\n  dataRetention: {\n    memoryDays: 30,\n    logsDays: 90,\n    auditDays: 2555 // 7 years for tax compliance\n  },\n  rightToDeletion: true\n});\n```\n\n### SOC 2 Readiness\n\nFor SOC 2 compliance:\n\n- [ ] Enable `auditLogging` with `verbose` level\n- [ ] Configure 90+ day log retention\n- [ ] Use per-agent API keys with rotation\n- [ ] Enable memory encryption\n- [ ] Configure alerting for policy violations\n\n## Security Monitoring\n\n### Alert Configuration\n\nSet up alerts for security events:\n\n```javascript\nagent.on('policy_violation', (event) => {\n  // Send alert to security team\n  await sendSecurityAlert({\n    severity: 'high',\n    agentId: event.agentId,\n    violation: event.details,\n    timestamp: event.timestamp\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### Anomaly Detection\n\nMonitor for unusual patterns:\n\n- High-frequency API calls\n- Access to unusual domains\n- Memory consumption spikes\n- Policy violation attempts\n\n## Production Security Checklist\n\n- [ ] Per-agent API keys with minimal permissions\n- [ ] Key rotation scheduled (90 days recommended)\n- [ ] Memory encryption enabled for sensitive data\n- [ ] Strict behavioral policies configured\n- [ ] Audit logging at `verbose` level\n- [ ] 90+ day log retention configured\n- [ ] Network policies restricting outbound access\n- [ ] Security alerts configured\n- [ ] Anomaly detection enabled\n- [ ] GDPR/SOC 2 controls implemented if required","src/content/docs/agents/security.mdx","8d5411cbd96bcc4c","api/authentication",{"id":78,"data":80,"body":86,"filePath":87,"digest":88,"rendered":89},{"title":81,"description":82,"editUrl":8,"head":83,"template":10,"sidebar":84,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Authentication","FunctionFly API authentication methods",[],{"hidden":13,"attrs":85},{},"# Authentication\n\nFunctionFly supports multiple authentication methods for API access.\n\n## API Key Authentication\n\nThe most common method for programmatic access:\n\n```http\nAuthorization: Bearer \u003Cyour-api-key>\n```\n\n## OAuth Authentication\n\nFor user-based authentication:\n\n```http\nGET /v1/auth/oauth/providers\nGET /v1/auth/oauth/url?provider=github&redirect_uri=...\n```\n\n## Session Authentication\n\nFor dashboard and web applications:\n\n```http\nPOST /v1/auth/login\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"email\": \"user@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"password\"\n}\n```\n\n## Refresh Token\n\nRefresh an expired access token:\n\n```http\nPOST /v1/auth/refresh\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"refresh_token\": \"...\"\n}\n```\n\n## Rate Limits\n\n| Endpoint Category | Limit |\n|-------------------|-------|\n| Authentication | 5 requests/minute |\n| General API | 60 requests/minute |","src/content/docs/api/authentication.md","459b6c6d8c2731b3",{"html":90,"metadata":91},"\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h1\">\u003Ch1 id=\"authentication\">Authentication\u003C/h1>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#authentication\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Authentication”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>FunctionFly supports multiple authentication methods for API access.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"api-key-authentication\">API Key Authentication\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#api-key-authentication\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “API Key Authentication”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>