/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">ffly\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">deploy\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cdiv class=\"copy\">\u003Cdiv aria-live=\"polite\">\u003C/div>\u003Cbutton title=\"Copy to clipboard\" data-copied=\"Copied!\" data-code=\"go install github.com/functionfly/functionfly/cmd/fly@latestffly loginffly init my-functionffly deploy\">\u003Cdiv>\u003C/div>\u003C/button>\u003C/div>\u003C/figure>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"documentation\">Documentation\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#documentation\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Documentation”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>Browse our documentation sections:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Getting Started\u003C/strong> - Quick start guides and installation\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Core Concepts\u003C/strong> - Functions, CLI, and deployment\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Trust &#x26; Security\u003C/strong> - Trust API and security protocols\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>",{"headings":2769,"localImagePaths":2775,"remoteImagePaths":2776,"frontmatter":2777,"imagePaths":2783},[2770,2771,2772],{"depth":25,"slug":465,"text":466},{"depth":25,"slug":665,"text":666},{"depth":25,"slug":2773,"text":2774},"documentation","Documentation",[],[],{"title":2736,"description":2737,"hero":2778},{"title":2740,"tagline":2741,"actions":2779},[2780,2781,2782],{"text":2744,"link":2745,"icon":2749,"variant":2746},{"text":2751,"link":2752,"icon":2755,"variant":2753},{"text":2757,"link":2758,"icon":2760,"variant":2753},[],"open-source-strategy",{"id":2784,"data":2786,"body":2791,"filePath":2792,"digest":2793,"rendered":2794},{"title":2787,"editUrl":8,"head":2788,"template":10,"sidebar":2789,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"OPEN SOURCE STRATEGY",[],{"hidden":13,"attrs":2790},{},"# Open Source Strategy: What to Publish and Monorepo vs Split\n\nThis doc recommends **what to open source** and whether to keep a **single monorepo** or **split** into public + private repos.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendation: **Single public monorepo**\n\n**Open the whole repo** (core platform + deploy config + docs), with these rules:\n\n| Publish | Keep out of repo (or use placeholders) |\n|--------|---------------------------------------|\n| All of `cmd/`, `internal/`, `web/`, `migrations/`, `runtimes/`, `functions/`, `packaging/` | Real credentials (already in `.env*` and gitignore) |\n| All of `deploy/` as **reference config** (Caddy, edge scripts, DB examples) | Real VPS IPs in scripts (see below: use env or placeholders) |\n| All of `docs/` and `plans/` (generic guides, architecture) | Runbooks that contain real connection strings (keep those in a private runbook or secrets manager) |\n| `*.env.example` only; never commit `.env`, `.env.production`, `deploy/database/production.env` | TLS private keys; `deploy/edge/certs-in/`, `certs-out/` (already gitignored) |\n\n**Why monorepo:**\n\n- One place for code, config, and docs. Contributors can run and deploy from the same tree.\n- Your product (FunctionFly) is the platform; the deploy layout is useful reference for self-hosters and for your own ops.\n- No sync burden between a “core” repo and a “deploy” repo.\n- Splitting only makes sense if you have **strict** need to hide infra (exact VPS IPs, internal runbooks); then you’d move only those bits (see “If you split” below).\n\n---\n\n## Before going public: one more hardening step\n\n**VPS IPs are currently hardcoded** in a few places. For a public repo, prefer **not** exposing your actual edge server IPs.\n\n| Location | Current | Change |\n|----------|---------|--------|\n| `internal/monitoring/edge_stats.go` | `defaultEdgeNodes` = two real IPs | Use **env-only default**: if `EDGE_NODES` is unset, show no nodes (or a placeholder). Remove hardcoded IPs. |\n| `.env.example` | Comment lists the two IPs | Replace with: `# EDGE_NODES=host1:Region A,host2:Region B` (no example IPs). |\n| `deploy/edge/upload-certs.sh` | `NODES=( \"217...\" \"209...\" )` | Source from env, e.g. `EDGE_VPS_NODES` (space-separated), with no default in repo. |\n| `deploy/edge/upload-certs-windows.ps1` | Same IPs | Same: read from env. |\n| `deploy/edge/README-CERTS.md` | Instructions with real IPs | Use placeholders: “Replace `EDGE_VPS_NODE_1` and `EDGE_VPS_NODE_2` with your node IPs.” |\n| `deploy/edge/vps-deploy.sh` | Comment with IPs | “Run on each edge VPS (set EDGE_VPS_NODES or pass host as arg).” |\n| `deploy/dns/cloudflare-geo-dns.json` | Real IPs in geo targets | **Option A:** Add to `.gitignore` and commit `cloudflare-geo-dns.example.json` with placeholders. **Option B:** Keep in repo if that DNS config is for a public demo; otherwise use Option A. |\n\nAfter this, the public repo contains no real infrastructure addresses; only your domain names (e.g. `functionfly.com`, `api.functionfly.com`) remain, which are fine for a product repo.\n\n---\n\n## If you split (public core + private ops)\n\nUse this only if you **must** keep exact edge topology, runbooks, and deploy details private.\n\n| Public repo | Private repo |\n|------------|--------------|\n| `cmd/`, `internal/`, `web/`, `migrations/`, `runtimes/`, `functions/`, `packaging/` | `deploy/` (or at least `deploy/edge/`, `deploy/database/` with real envs) |\n| `docs/` that are user-facing or generic (QUICK_START, PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT, SECURITY, OBJECT_STORAGE, etc.) | `docs/` that are runbooks (e.g. STAGING with real credentials, DISASTER_RECOVERY_RUNBOOK, internal playbooks) |\n| `*.env.example` only | Real `.env.staging`, `.env.production`, `deploy/database/production.env` |\n| Generic deploy examples (e.g. Caddy with `your-domain.com`) | Your actual Caddyfiles and scripts with real IPs and functionfly.com |\n\n**Pros:** Real VPS IPs, exact Caddy config, and runbooks never touch the public repo.  \n**Cons:** Two repos to maintain; deploy config can drift from code; contributors don’t see “how you deploy” end-to-end.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Recommended:** Single **public monorepo**, with no secrets (done), no real credentials in docs (done), and **VPS IPs moved to env or placeholders** so nothing sensitive is exposed.\n- **Optional:** A small **private** repo or wiki for “runbooks only” (real connection strings, incident playbooks) while the main repo stays the single source of code and reference deploy config.\n- **Split only if** you have a hard requirement to hide all deploy topology and runbooks; then use the table above to decide what lives in each repo.","src/content/docs/open-source-strategy.md","c4afe25e56f6e379",{"html":2795,"metadata":2796},"\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h1\">\u003Ch1 id=\"open-source-strategy-what-to-publish-and-monorepo-vs-split\">Open Source Strategy: What to Publish and Monorepo vs Split\u003C/h1>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#open-source-strategy-what-to-publish-and-monorepo-vs-split\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Open Source Strategy: What to Publish and Monorepo vs Split”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>This doc recommends \u003Cstrong>what to open source\u003C/strong> and whether to keep a \u003Cstrong>single monorepo\u003C/strong> or \u003Cstrong>split\u003C/strong> into public + private repos.\u003C/p>\n\u003Chr>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"recommendation-single-public-monorepo\">Recommendation: \u003Cstrong>Single public monorepo\u003C/strong>\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#recommendation-single-public-monorepo\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Recommendation: Single public monorepo”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Open the whole repo\u003C/strong> (core platform + deploy config + docs), with these rules:\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003Ctable>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Publish\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Keep out of repo (or use placeholders)\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>All of \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">cmd/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">internal/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">web/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">migrations/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">runtimes/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">functions/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">packaging/\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Real credentials (already in \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.env*\u003C/code> and gitignore)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>All of \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/\u003C/code> as \u003Cstrong>reference config\u003C/strong> (Caddy, edge scripts, DB examples)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Real VPS IPs in scripts (see below: use env or placeholders)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>All of \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">docs/\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">plans/\u003C/code> (generic guides, architecture)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Runbooks that contain real connection strings (keep those in a private runbook or secrets manager)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">*.env.example\u003C/code> only; never commit \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.env\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.env.production\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/database/production.env\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>TLS private keys; \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/edge/certs-in/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">certs-out/\u003C/code> (already gitignored)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Why monorepo:\u003C/strong>\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>One place for code, config, and docs. Contributors can run and deploy from the same tree.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Your product (FunctionFly) is the platform; the deploy layout is useful reference for self-hosters and for your own ops.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>No sync burden between a “core” repo and a “deploy” repo.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>Splitting only makes sense if you have \u003Cstrong>strict\u003C/strong> need to hide infra (exact VPS IPs, internal runbooks); then you’d move only those bits (see “If you split” below).\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Chr>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"before-going-public-one-more-hardening-step\">Before going public: one more hardening step\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#before-going-public-one-more-hardening-step\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Before going public: one more hardening step”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>VPS IPs are currently hardcoded\u003C/strong> in a few places. For a public repo, prefer \u003Cstrong>not\u003C/strong> exposing your actual edge server IPs.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003Ctable>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Location\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Current\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Change\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">internal/monitoring/edge_stats.go\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">defaultEdgeNodes\u003C/code> = two real IPs\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Use \u003Cstrong>env-only default\u003C/strong>: if \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">EDGE_NODES\u003C/code> is unset, show no nodes (or a placeholder). Remove hardcoded IPs.\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.env.example\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Comment lists the two IPs\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Replace with: \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\"># EDGE_NODES=host1:Region A,host2:Region B\u003C/code> (no example IPs).\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/edge/upload-certs.sh\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">NODES=( \"217...\" \"209...\" )\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Source from env, e.g. \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">EDGE_VPS_NODES\u003C/code> (space-separated), with no default in repo.\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/edge/upload-certs-windows.ps1\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Same IPs\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Same: read from env.\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/edge/README-CERTS.md\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Instructions with real IPs\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Use placeholders: “Replace \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">EDGE_VPS_NODE_1\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">EDGE_VPS_NODE_2\u003C/code> with your node IPs.”\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/edge/vps-deploy.sh\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Comment with IPs\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>“Run on each edge VPS (set EDGE_VPS_NODES or pass host as arg).”\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/dns/cloudflare-geo-dns.json\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Real IPs in geo targets\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Cstrong>Option A:\u003C/strong> Add to \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.gitignore\u003C/code> and commit \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">cloudflare-geo-dns.example.json\u003C/code> with placeholders. \u003Cstrong>Option B:\u003C/strong> Keep in repo if that DNS config is for a public demo; otherwise use Option A.\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n\u003Cp>After this, the public repo contains no real infrastructure addresses; only your domain names (e.g. \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">functionfly.com\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">api.functionfly.com\u003C/code>) remain, which are fine for a product repo.\u003C/p>\n\u003Chr>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"if-you-split-public-core--private-ops\">If you split (public core + private ops)\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#if-you-split-public-core--private-ops\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “If you split (public core + private ops)”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>Use this only if you \u003Cstrong>must\u003C/strong> keep exact edge topology, runbooks, and deploy details private.\u003C/p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003Ctable>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Public repo\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Private repo\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">cmd/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">internal/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">web/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">migrations/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">runtimes/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">functions/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">packaging/\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/\u003C/code> (or at least \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/edge/\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/database/\u003C/code> with real envs)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">docs/\u003C/code> that are user-facing or generic (QUICK_START, PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT, SECURITY, OBJECT_STORAGE, etc.)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">docs/\u003C/code> that are runbooks (e.g. STAGING with real credentials, DISASTER_RECOVERY_RUNBOOK, internal playbooks)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">*.env.example\u003C/code> only\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Real \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.env.staging\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">.env.production\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">deploy/database/production.env\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Generic deploy examples (e.g. Caddy with \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">your-domain.com\u003C/code>)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Your actual Caddyfiles and scripts with real IPs and functionfly.com\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Pros:\u003C/strong> Real VPS IPs, exact Caddy config, and runbooks never touch the public repo.\u003Cbr>\n\u003Cstrong>Cons:\u003C/strong> Two repos to maintain; deploy config can drift from code; contributors don’t see “how you deploy” end-to-end.\u003C/p>\n\u003Chr>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"summary\">Summary\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#summary\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Summary”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Recommended:\u003C/strong> Single \u003Cstrong>public monorepo\u003C/strong>, with no secrets (done), no real credentials in docs (done), and \u003Cstrong>VPS IPs moved to env or placeholders\u003C/strong> so nothing sensitive is exposed.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Optional:\u003C/strong> A small \u003Cstrong>private\u003C/strong> repo or wiki for “runbooks only” (real connection strings, incident playbooks) while the main repo stays the single source of code and reference deploy config.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Split only if\u003C/strong> you have a hard requirement to hide all deploy topology and runbooks; then use the table above to decide what lives in each repo.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>",{"headings":2797,"localImagePaths":2813,"remoteImagePaths":2814,"frontmatter":2815,"imagePaths":2816},[2798,2801,2804,2807,2810],{"depth":12,"slug":2799,"text":2800},"open-source-strategy-what-to-publish-and-monorepo-vs-split","Open Source Strategy: What to Publish and Monorepo vs Split",{"depth":25,"slug":2802,"text":2803},"recommendation-single-public-monorepo","Recommendation: Single public monorepo",{"depth":25,"slug":2805,"text":2806},"before-going-public-one-more-hardening-step","Before going public: one more hardening step",{"depth":25,"slug":2808,"text":2809},"if-you-split-public-core--private-ops","If you split (public core + private ops)",{"depth":25,"slug":2811,"text":2812},"summary","Summary",[],[],{"title":2787},[],{"id":271,"data":2818,"body":2824,"filePath":2825,"digest":2826,"rendered":2827},{"title":2819,"description":2820,"editUrl":8,"head":2821,"template":10,"sidebar":2822,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Pricing Overview","FunctionFly pricing plans and options overview.",[],{"order":12,"hidden":13,"attrs":2823},{},"FunctionFly offers transparent, scalable pricing for every stage of growth—from hobby projects to enterprise deployments.\n\n## Our Products\n\n- **[Serverless Functions](/pricing/features-by-tier/#serverless-functions)** — Deploy code to the edge. Free tier available.\n- **[StateFabric](/pricing/features-by-tier/#statefabric)** — Durable state for stateless functions.\n- **[Agents](/pricing/features-by-tier/#agents)** — Autonomous AI with memory and policies.\n- **[Backend-in-a-Box Bundles](/pricing/features-by-tier/#backend-in-a-box-bundles)** — Pre-configured backends in one click.\n\n## See All Features by Tier\n\nFor a detailed breakdown of every feature and limit across all plans, see **[Features by Tier](/pricing/features-by-tier/)**.\n\n## Common Questions\n\n**Do you offer a free trial?**  \nYes. All paid plans include a 14-day free trial. No credit card required.\n\n**Can I change plans?**  \nUpgrade or downgrade anytime. Upgrades apply immediately; downgrades at the end of your billing cycle.\n\n**Is there a pay-as-you-go option?**  \nYes. Pay only for what you use with no monthly commitment.\n\n**Need enterprise pricing?**  \n[Contact our sales team](https://functionfly.com/contact) for custom SLAs, volume discounts, and on-premise deployment.","src/content/docs/pricing/index.md","6f95db803702d3f3",{"html":2828,"metadata":2829},"\u003Cp>FunctionFly offers transparent, scalable pricing for every stage of growth—from hobby projects to enterprise deployments.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"our-products\">Our Products\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#our-products\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Our Products”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"/pricing/features-by-tier/#serverless-functions\">Serverless Functions\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> — Deploy code to the edge. Free tier available.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"/pricing/features-by-tier/#statefabric\">StateFabric\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> — Durable state for stateless functions.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"/pricing/features-by-tier/#agents\">Agents\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> — Autonomous AI with memory and policies.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"/pricing/features-by-tier/#backend-in-a-box-bundles\">Backend-in-a-Box Bundles\u003C/a>\u003C/strong> — Pre-configured backends in one click.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"see-all-features-by-tier\">See All Features by Tier\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#see-all-features-by-tier\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “See All Features by Tier”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>For a detailed breakdown of every feature and limit across all plans, see \u003Cstrong>\u003Ca href=\"/pricing/features-by-tier/\">Features by Tier\u003C/a>\u003C/strong>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"common-questions\">Common Questions\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#common-questions\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Common Questions”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Do you offer a free trial?\u003C/strong>\u003Cbr>\nYes. All paid plans include a 14-day free trial. No credit card required.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Can I change plans?\u003C/strong>\u003Cbr>\nUpgrade or downgrade anytime. Upgrades apply immediately; downgrades at the end of your billing cycle.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Is there a pay-as-you-go option?\u003C/strong>\u003Cbr>\nYes. Pay only for what you use with no monthly commitment.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Need enterprise pricing?\u003C/strong>\u003Cbr>\n\u003Ca href=\"https://functionfly.com/contact\">Contact our sales team\u003C/a> for custom SLAs, volume discounts, and on-premise deployment.\u003C/p>",{"headings":2830,"localImagePaths":2840,"remoteImagePaths":2841,"frontmatter":2842,"imagePaths":2844},[2831,2834,2837],{"depth":25,"slug":2832,"text":2833},"our-products","Our Products",{"depth":25,"slug":2835,"text":2836},"see-all-features-by-tier","See All Features by Tier",{"depth":25,"slug":2838,"text":2839},"common-questions","Common Questions",[],[],{"title":2819,"description":2820,"sidebar":2843},{"order":12},[],"pricing/features-by-tier",{"id":2845,"data":2847,"body":2853,"filePath":2854,"digest":2855,"deferredRender":8},{"title":2848,"description":2849,"editUrl":8,"head":2850,"template":10,"sidebar":2851,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Features by Tier","Everything FunctionFly offers, organized by plan tier. Find what fits you—from free hobby projects to enterprise scale.",[],{"order":25,"hidden":13,"attrs":2852},{},"import { Card, CardGrid } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';\n\nNot sure which plan fits your project? This page lists **everything** FunctionFly offers, organized by product area and tier. Start free and upgrade only when you need more.\n\n\u003CCardGrid>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Functions\" icon=\"rocket\">\n    Deploy serverless code to the edge\n  \u003C/Card>\n  \u003CCard title=\"StateFabric\" icon=\"database\">\n    Durable state for stateless functions\n  \u003C/Card>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Agents\" icon=\"seti:custom\">\n    Autonomous AI with memory and policies\n  \u003C/Card>\n  \u003CCard title=\"Bundles\" icon=\"box\">\n    Pre-built backends in one click\n  \u003C/Card>\n\u003C/CardGrid>\n\n---\n\n## Serverless Functions\n\nDeploy code in Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Go, Rust, and more to 35+ edge locations worldwide.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter ($24/mo) | Professional ($79/mo) | Enterprise ($299/mo) |\n|---------|------|------------------|----------------------|----------------------|\n| **Functions** | 1 | 5 | 25 | Unlimited |\n| **Cloud Providers** | 2 | 3 | 5 | All (Cloudflare, Vercel, Fly.io, AWS Lambda, Deno, etc.) |\n| **Monthly Requests** | 100,000 | 1 million | 10 million | 100 million+ |\n| **Overage Billing** | Hard stop | $0.15 per 1K calls | $0.08 per 1K calls | $0.05 per 1K calls |\n| **Custom Domains** | — | 1 | 5 | Unlimited |\n| **SLA Uptime** | Best effort | Best effort | 99.9% | 99.99% |\n| **Team Collaboration** | — | — | Included | Included |\n| **Analytics** | Basic usage | Basic usage | Advanced | Custom dashboards |\n| **Support** | Community (Discord/GitHub) | Email | Priority | Dedicated |\n| **Annual Discount** | — | 20% off | 20% off | 30% off + volume pricing |\n\n**Also included on all tiers:**\n- **Multi-Provider Deployment** — Deploy to multiple cloud providers with intelligent failover\n- **Edge Functions** — Ultra-low latency execution at the edge via WASM runtime\n- **AI Composer** — Generate functions with AI (all tiers, usage-based limits)\n- **Function Remix** — Fork and remix community functions from the registry\n- **GitHub Import** — Import functions directly from GitHub repositories\n- **Deploy Keys** — Secure automated deployments without passwords\n- **CI/CD Integration** — GitHub Actions and pipeline automation\n\n**Free tier best for:** Personal demos, learning, small side projects.  \n**Starter best for:** Side projects and MVPs that need a few functions.  \n**Professional best for:** Growing SaaS apps and teams.  \n**Enterprise best for:** Large-scale apps needing custom SLAs and dedicated support.\n\n---\n\n## StateFabric\n\nAdd durable state to your serverless functions—shopping carts, sessions, configs, and more.\n\n| Feature | Sandbox (Free) | Starter ($19/mo) | Pro ($99/mo) | Business ($499/mo) | Enterprise (Custom) |\n|---------|---------------|------------------|--------------|--------------------|---------------------|\n| **State Objects** | 1 | 5 | 50 | 500 | Unlimited |\n| **Event Storage** | 1 GB | 10 GB | 100 GB | 1 TB | Unlimited |\n| **State Operations** | 10,000/mo | 100,000/mo | 1 million/mo | 10 million/mo | Unlimited |\n| **Snapshot Retention** | 7 days | 30 days | 90 days | 180 days | 365 days |\n| **Replay Engine** | — | Limited | Fast + API | Full | Export + custom |\n| **Multi-Region** | — | — | — | Yes | Yes + edge replication |\n| **Hot Cache Tier** | — | — | Included | Dedicated | Dedicated |\n| **Support** | Community | Email | Priority | SLA | Dedicated |\n\n**Add-ons available on paid plans:**\n- Hot Cache Booster — $49/mo per 5 GB (faster reads/replay)\n- Advanced Security Pack — $99/mo (SOC2 logs, key rotation, audit streams)\n- AI Memory Pack — $149/mo (vector index, embeddings storage)\n- Advanced Insights — $79/mo (cost forecasting, anomaly detection)\n\n---\n\n## Agents\n\nAutonomous AI agents that can execute tasks, remember context, and follow safety policies.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter ($24/mo) | Scale ($79/mo) | Enterprise ($499/mo) |\n|---------|------|------------------|----------------|----------------------|\n| **Agents** | — | 10 | 100 | 500+ |\n| **AI / Tool Calls** | Limited discovery | 100,000/mo | 1 million/mo | 5 million/mo+ |\n| **Concurrent Agents** | — | 10 | 100 | 500+ |\n| **Calls per Minute** | — | 100 | 500 | 2,000+ |\n| **State Writes / Hour** | — | 100 | 10,000 | 50,000+ |\n| **Trust Verification** | Basic scores + trust levels | Verification + signing gates | Advanced trust routing | Custom certification flows |\n| **Audit Trail** | Limited | Extended | 90 days | Configurable (compliance) |\n| **Policy Templates** | Basic filters | Starter pack | Org policy packs | Custom trust policies |\n| **Memory Storage** | — | 10 GB | 100 GB | 500 GB+ |\n| **Log Retention** | — | 30 days | 90 days | 1 year |\n| **Support** | Community | Email | Priority | Dedicated + 24/7 |\n\n**Advanced agent capabilities (paid tiers):**\n- **Agent Swarm** — Coordinate multiple agents working together\n- **Agent Evolution** — Self-improving agents that learn from execution\n- **SEBG (Self-Evolving Behavior Graph)** — Dynamic behavior evolution\n- **Daemon Mode** — Background agents that run continuously\n\n**Agent Enterprise (Ultimate tier — Custom pricing):**\n- Unlimited AI calls, agents, and concurrency\n- Unlimited state writes and memory storage\n- 1-year log retention\n- Dedicated infrastructure\n- Custom SLA + 24/7 support\n- On-premise deployment option\n\n---\n\n## Backend-in-a-Box Bundles\n\nPre-configured backends for common app types. One click deploys Auth, Payments, Database, and more.\n\n| Bundle | Price | Best For | What's Inside |\n|--------|-------|----------|---------------|\n| **SaaS Starter** | $29/mo | Launching a SaaS product | Auth, User DB, Stripe payments, Email workflows, Analytics |\n| **Marketplace** | $49/mo | Multi-vendor platforms | Seller profiles, Listings, Payments split, Reviews, Admin tools |\n| **AI App** | $39/mo | AI-powered applications | LLM integrations, Vector DB, Prompt management, Usage tracking |\n\n**Founder Mode — Build free for 3 months:**\n- No credit card required to start\n- Free until you hit **100 users** or **$1K MRR**\n- 7-day grace period to add payment info after hitting the limit\n- Your data is never deleted\n\n---\n\n## Platform-Wide Features\n\nTools and capabilities available across the entire platform.\n\n### Secrets Vault (Zero-Knowledge)\n\nYour secrets are encrypted **in your browser** before they ever reach our servers. We cannot read them.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **Secrets** | — | 10 | 50 | 10,000+ |\n| **Tokens per Secret** | — | 5 | 20 | 100+ |\n| **Zero-Knowledge Encryption** | — | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n\n### Time Machine (Execution Replay)\n\nReplay past function executions to debug issues, verify behavior, and reconcile state.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **Replay Window** | 24 hours | 72 hours | 30 days | 90 days |\n| **Executions per Replay** | 100 | 1,000 | 10,000 | 100,000 |\n| **Concurrent Replays** | 1 | 1 | 3 | 10 |\n| **Diff Reports** | Basic text | Text diffs | Full structured | Full structured |\n| **Auto Reconciliation** | — | — | Dry-run only | Dry-run + Live |\n| **Audit Certificates** | — | — | — | SOC2 / HIPAA ready |\n\n### Registry & Marketplace\n\nPublish, share, and discover serverless functions and agents.\n\n| Feature | Free | Paid Tiers |\n|---------|------|------------|\n| **Browse Registry** | Yes | Yes |\n| **Publish Functions** | Yes | Yes |\n| **Verified Publisher Badge** | — | Available with verification |\n| **Trust Tiers** | Basic | Basic, High, Enterprise |\n| **Function Remix** | Yes | Yes |\n| **Ratings & Reviews** | Yes | Yes |\n\n### Trust & Verification\n\nSecurity and trust layers for production deployments.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **Malware Scanning** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Signature Verification** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Trust Scores** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Trust API Access** | Basic | Usage-based | Higher limits | Enterprise scale |\n| **HMAC Request Signing** | — | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Per-API-Key Cost Tracking** | — | — | Yes | Yes + budgets & alerts |\n\n### Function DNA (Evolution Engine)\n\nYour functions can evolve automatically. The DNA engine analyzes execution patterns, proposes AI-generated mutations, and deploys improvements via canary releases.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **DNA Profile & Insights** | Basic | Full | Full + predictive | Full + custom rules |\n| **Auto-Evolution** | — | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Mutation Proposals** | — | Up to 5/day | Up to 10/day | Unlimited |\n| **Canary Deployments** | — | 10% default | Custom % | Custom % + auto-rollback |\n| **Mutation Cost** | — | 50 credits each | 50 credits each | 50 credits each |\n| **Accept/Reject Variants** | — | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n\n**How it works:**\n1. The DNA engine monitors your function's execution\n2. AI proposes code mutations (optimizations, bug fixes, features)\n3. You review diffs and accept or reject each variant\n4. Accepted mutations deploy via canary with automatic rollback on errors\n\n### Function Runtime Graph (FRG)\n\nBuild complex workflows by visually connecting functions in a drag-and-drop graph editor. No code required.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **Visual Graph Editor** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **3D Graph View** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **AI Workflow Assistant** | Limited | Full | Full | Full |\n| **Test Runner** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Version Control** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Live Collaboration** | — | — | Yes | Yes |\n| **Execution Monitoring** | Basic | Basic | Advanced | Real-time |\n\n### Apps Platform\n\nBuild and deploy full applications composed of functions, state, and integrations.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **Apps** | — | 3 | 10 | Unlimited |\n| **Custom Domains per App** | — | 1 | 5 | Unlimited |\n| **App Analytics** | — | Basic | Advanced | Custom |\n\n### Developer Certification\n\nEarn verifiable credentials that prove your serverless expertise. Certified developers can charge premium pricing in the marketplace.\n\n| Tier | Price | What You Get |\n|------|-------|--------------|\n| **Associate** | Free | Entry-level certification with knowledge test |\n| **Professional** | $49 | Advanced exam with practical challenges (Coming Soon) |\n| **Architect** | $99 | Expert-level certification with design challenges (Coming Soon) |\n\n**Benefits of certification:**\n- Verifiable LinkedIn-ready credentials\n- Up to 40% more pricing power in the marketplace\n- Industry recognition\n- Public credential verification page\n\n### Wallet & Credits\n\nA platform wallet for paying per-use features like DNA mutations, function remixes, and premium API calls.\n\n| Feature | All Tiers |\n|---------|-----------|\n| **Wallet** | Yes (add funds anytime) |\n| **Credit Purchases** | Yes ($1 = 100 credits) |\n| **DNA Mutations** | 50 credits each |\n| **Function Remixes** | Varies by function |\n| **Premium API Calls** | Usage-based |\n\n### Publisher Payouts & Affiliate\n\nMonetize your functions and earn from referrals.\n\n| Feature | Free | Paid Tiers |\n|---------|------|------------|\n| **Publish Paid Functions** | — | Yes (set price per call) |\n| **Publisher Revenue Share** | — | 70% of call revenue |\n| **Affiliate Program** | — | Yes (referral commissions) |\n| **Stripe Connect Payouts** | — | Yes (direct bank deposits) |\n| **Payout Scheduling** | — | Weekly / Monthly |\n\n### Team & Collaboration\n\nInvite team members and manage access across your organization.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|\n| **Team Members** | 1 (solo) | 3 | 10 | Unlimited |\n| **Role-Based Access** | — | Basic | Advanced | Custom roles |\n| **Member Invites** | — | Email invites | Email invites | SSO + SAML |\n| **MFA Enforcement** | — | — | Optional | Required |\n| **Audit Logs** | — | — | 90 days | 1 year+ |\n\n**Roles available:** Owner, Admin, Member, Viewer\n\n### Function Consciousness\n\nAI-powered insights that monitor your functions and suggest improvements automatically.\n\n| Feature | Free | Starter | Professional | Enterprise | Agent Enterprise |\n|---------|------|---------|--------------|------------|------------------|\n| **Basic Consciousness** | — | — | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Advanced Consciousness** | — | — | — | Yes | Yes |\n| **Autonomous Consciousness** | — | — | — | — | Yes |\n| **Lookback Window** | — | — | 7 days | 30 days | Unlimited |\n| **Daily Digest** | — | — | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| **Real-time Alerts** | — | — | — | Yes | Yes |\n| **Predictive Fixes** | — | — | — | Yes | Yes |\n| **Self-Healing** | — | — | — | — | Yes |\n\n**Consciousness tiers explained:**\n- **Basic** (Professional+): Daily digest of function health, basic insights, 7-day lookback\n- **Advanced** (Enterprise+): Real-time monitoring, predictive failure detection, auto-fix suggestions, 30-day lookback\n- **Autonomous** (Agent Enterprise): Self-healing functions, unlimited lookback, automatic remediation\n\n### Notifications & System Status\n\n| Feature | All Tiers |\n|---------|-----------|\n| **In-App Notifications** | Yes |\n| **Email Alerts** | Yes |\n| **System Status Page** | Yes (public) |\n| **Incident Alerts** | Yes |\n| **Webhook Notifications** | Professional+ |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Comparison: Which Tier Is Right for You?\n\n| If you are... | Start with | Upgrade when... |\n|---------------|------------|-----------------|\n| Learning or building a personal demo | **Free** | You need more than 1 function or 100K requests |\n| Building a side project or MVP | **Starter** | You need team collaboration or 99.9% SLA |\n| Running a growing SaaS or business | **Professional** | You need unlimited scale, custom SLAs, or dedicated support |\n| A large company with compliance needs | **Enterprise** | — |\n| Building a SaaS, marketplace, or AI app fast | **Backend-in-a-Box Bundle** | You outgrow the pre-configured setup |\n\n---\n\n## Common Questions\n\n**Do all paid plans have a free trial?**  \nYes. Every paid plan includes a 14-day free trial. No credit card required to start.\n\n**Can I change plans later?**  \nYes. Upgrade or downgrade anytime. Upgrades apply immediately; downgrades take effect at the end of your billing cycle.\n\n**What happens if I exceed my limits?**  \nWe notify you before you hit limits. Free plans have a hard stop. Paid plans include generous allowances with overage billing—you only pay for what you use beyond your quota.\n\n**Is there a pay-as-you-go option?**  \nYes. You can use the Pay-as-you-go tier with no monthly commitment. You pay a slightly higher per-request rate but only for what you use.\n\n**Do you offer annual discounts?**  \nYes. Starter and Professional plans save 20% when billed annually. Enterprise plans save 30% and include volume-based pricing.\n\n**What is Founder Mode?**  \nFounder Mode lets you use Backend-in-a-Box bundles free for 3 months (or until you hit 100 users / $1K MRR). It is designed to help early-stage startups launch with zero upfront cost.\n\n**How do DNA mutation credits work?**  \nEach accepted mutation costs 50 credits from your wallet. Rejected mutations are free. You can buy credits starting at $1 for 100 credits.\n\n**Are certifications free?**  \nThe Associate certification is free. Professional and Architect tiers have exam fees ($49 and $99).\n\n---\n\n## Need Help Choosing?\n\n- [Pricing Overview](/pricing/) — See plan cards and start a trial\n- [Contact Sales](https://functionfly.com/contact) — Talk to our team about Enterprise or custom needs\n- [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/functionfly/functionfly/discussions) — Ask the community","src/content/docs/pricing/features-by-tier.mdx","11c3729f84ac8867","providers",{"id":2856,"data":2858,"body":2864,"filePath":2865,"digest":2866,"rendered":2867},{"title":2859,"description":2860,"editUrl":8,"head":2861,"template":10,"sidebar":2862,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Providers","Deploy FunctionFly functions to your preferred cloud provider",[],{"hidden":13,"attrs":2863},{},"FunctionFly supports deploying your functions to multiple cloud providers. Each provider offers unique features, regional coverage, and pricing models.\n\n## Supported Providers\n\n| Provider | ID | Description | Environment |\n|----------|-----|-------------|-------------|\n| [FunctionFly Edge](./functionfly-edge/environment) | `functionfly-edge` | Built-in global edge network with Trust API, Secrets Vault, StateFabric | [Docs](./functionfly-edge/environment) |\n| [Vercel](./vercel/environment) | `vercel` | Edge functions with global CDN, Next.js integration | [Docs](./vercel/environment) |\n| [Cloudflare Workers](./cloudflare-workers/environment) | `workers` | Ultra-low latency edge compute with Workers KV | [Docs](./cloudflare-workers/environment) |\n| [Fly.io](./fly-io/environment) | `fly` | Distributed apps with persistent volumes | [Docs](./fly-io/environment) |\n| [AWS Lambda](./aws-lambda/environment) | `aws-lambda` | Enterprise-grade serverless, deep AWS integration | [Docs](./aws-lambda/environment) |\n| [Deno Deploy](./deno-deploy/environment) | `deno-deploy` | Native TypeScript runtime with Deno KV | [Docs](./deno-deploy/environment) |\n\n## Quick Comparison\n\n| Best For | Provider |\n|----------|----------|\n| Fastest cold start | FunctionFly Edge (\u003C1ms) |\n| Most memory | AWS Lambda (10GB) |\n| Longest timeout | AWS Lambda (900s) |\n| Zero config | FunctionFly Edge |\n| Next.js projects | Vercel |\n| KV storage | Cloudflare Workers, Deno Deploy |\n| Persistent storage | Fly.io, AWS Lambda |\n| Enterprise scale | AWS Lambda |\n\n## Multi-Provider Deployment\n\nDeploy to multiple providers simultaneously for redundancy or geographic distribution:\n\n```jsonc\n// functionfly.jsonc\n{\n  \"providers\": [\"functionfly-edge\", \"vercel\", \"workers\"],\n  \"regions\": [\"us-east\", \"eu-west\", \"ap-south\"]\n}\n```\n\n## Getting Started\n\n1. **FunctionFly Edge**: No setup required - just run `ffly deploy`\n2. **Other providers**: Connect your account in the dashboard under Settings → Providers\n3. **Deploy**: Use `ffly deploy --provider \u003Cprovider-id>` or set in config\n\nSee individual provider guides for detailed setup instructions.","src/content/docs/providers/index.md","4ab9853b4047e0d5",{"html":2868,"metadata":2869},"\u003Cp>FunctionFly supports deploying your functions to multiple cloud providers. Each provider offers unique features, regional coverage, and pricing models.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"supported-providers\">Supported Providers\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#supported-pro