a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “🆘 Common Issues”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Issue:\u003C/strong> \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">docker: command not found\u003C/code>\u003Cbr>\n\u003Cstrong>Fix:\u003C/strong> \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh\u003C/code>\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Issue:\u003C/strong> Containers failing to start\u003Cbr>\n\u003Cstrong>Fix:\u003C/strong> Check logs: \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">docker compose logs -f\u003C/code>\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Issue:\u003C/strong> Cannot connect to Server 2 from Server 1\u003Cbr>\n\u003Cstrong>Fix:\u003C/strong> Verify UFW rules: \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">ufw allow from &#x3C;server1-ip>\u003C/code>\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Issue:\u003C/strong> SSL certificate errors\u003Cbr>\n\u003Cstrong>Fix:\u003C/strong> Ensure Cloudflare SSL mode is “Full (strict)”\u003C/p>\n\u003Chr>\n\u003Cp>\u003Cem>Deploy time: ~5 minutes | For detailed configuration, see \u003Ca href=\"./PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT.md\">PRODUCTION_DEPLOYMENT.md\u003C/a>\u003C/em>\u003C/p>",{"headings":3141,"localImagePaths":3187,"remoteImagePaths":3188,"frontmatter":3189,"imagePaths":3190},[3142,3145,3148,3151,3154,3157,3160,3163,3166,3169,3172,3175,3178,3181,3184],{"depth":12,"slug":3143,"text":3144},"-functionfly-production-quick-start","⚡ FunctionFly Production Quick Start",{"depth":25,"slug":3146,"text":3147},"-prerequisites-️-30s","📋 Prerequisites ⏱️ 30s",{"depth":25,"slug":3149,"text":3150},"-tldr-deploy-️-2min","🚀 TL;DR Deploy ⏱️ 2min",{"depth":25,"slug":3152,"text":3153},"-step-by-step-quick-deploy-️-5min","📖 Step-by-Step Quick Deploy ⏱️ 5min",{"depth":61,"slug":3155,"text":3156},"step-1-clone--env-setup-️-1min","Step 1: Clone & Env Setup ⏱️ 1min",{"depth":61,"slug":3158,"text":3159},"step-2-deploy-app-stack-server-1-️-2min","Step 2: Deploy App Stack (Server 1) ⏱️ 2min",{"depth":61,"slug":3161,"text":3162},"step-3-deploy-runtime-stack-server-2-️-1min","Step 3: Deploy Runtime Stack (Server 2) ⏱️ 1min",{"depth":61,"slug":3164,"text":3165},"step-4-verify-deployment-️-1min","Step 4: Verify Deployment ⏱️ 1min",{"depth":25,"slug":3167,"text":3168},"-quick-verification-commands","🔍 Quick Verification Commands",{"depth":61,"slug":3170,"text":3171},"container-status","Container Status",{"depth":61,"slug":3173,"text":3174},"test-function-deployment","Test Function Deployment",{"depth":61,"slug":3176,"text":3177},"database-connection-neon","Database Connection (Neon)",{"depth":25,"slug":3179,"text":3180},"-next-steps","📚 Next Steps",{"depth":25,"slug":3182,"text":3183},"-cost-summary","💰 Cost Summary",{"depth":25,"slug":3185,"text":3186},"-common-issues","🆘 Common Issues",[],[],{"title":3131},[],"roadmap",{"id":3191,"data":3193,"body":3199,"filePath":3200,"digest":3201,"deferredRender":8},{"title":3194,"description":3195,"editUrl":8,"head":3196,"template":10,"sidebar":3197,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Roadmap","What's coming next to FunctionFly. Stay informed about upcoming features, improvements, and releases.",[],{"order":61,"hidden":13,"attrs":3198},{},"We believe in being transparent about what we're building. This page shows what we're working on, what's coming soon, and what's on our radar. We update it regularly as plans evolve.\n\n## Recently Shipped\n\n*Features and improvements we've released most recently.*\n\n| Version | Date | Highlights |\n|---------|------|------------|\n| **v1.5** | May 2026 | **Invite-only launch** — Discord community launch ([discord.gg/FGnseK9Bp](https://discord.gg/FGnseK9Bp)), public beta opened with invite-only access |\n| **v1.4** | April 2026 | Function DNA evolution engine, FRG visual workflow editor, Backend-in-a-Box bundles |\n| **v1.3** | March 2026 | Agent memory systems, Consciousness dashboard, Hot Cache for StateFabric |\n| **v1.2** | February 2026 | StateFabric general availability, Agent Swarm coordination |\n| **v1.1** | January 2026 | Multi-provider deployment, Trust API |\n\n---\n\n## In Development\n\n*Currently being built. Expected in the next 1-3 months.*\n\n### Functions & Runtime\n\n- **WASM Runtime v2** — Improved cold start times, broader language support, and better debugging tools — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-beta\">Beta\u003C/span>\n- **Multi-region Auto-failover** — Automatic traffic routing when a region experiences issues — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Function Pipeline Stages** — Build → Test → Deploy pipelines with stage gates — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Enhanced Time Machine** — 90-day replay window with structured diff reports and audit certificates — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n\n### StateFabric\n\n- **State Triggers** — Execute functions automatically when state changes — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Cross-Fabric Queries** — Query across multiple state objects with JOIN support — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-planned\">Planned\u003C/span>\n- **GraphQL State API** — Query state with GraphQL alongside REST — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-design\">Design\u003C/span>\n\n### Agents & AI\n\n- **Agent Marketplace** — Pre-built agents ready to deploy — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Multi-Agent Swarms** — Coordinate multiple agents to work together on complex tasks — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Agent-to-Agent Protocol** — Standardized communication between agents — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-design\">Design\u003C/span>\n- **Consciousness Dashboard** — Unified view of function health, predictions, and auto-fix status — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n\n### Developer Tools\n\n- **VS Code Extension** — Full-featured IDE integration for function development — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **GitHub Actions OIDC** — Secure CI/CD without long-lived secrets — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-testing\">Testing\u003C/span>\n- **Local Dev Environment** — Docker-based local stack with hot reload — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Terraform Provider** — Infrastructure-as-Code for FunctionFly resources — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-planned\">Planned\u003C/span>\n\n### Platform & Enterprise\n\n- **SOC 2 Type II Audit** — Third-party security certification — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **SAML SSO** — Enterprise identity provider integration — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span>\n- **Private Registry** — Host functions internally within an organization — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-design\">Design\u003C/span>\n- **Audit Log Streaming** — Real-time delivery of audit events to your SIEM — \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-planned\">Planned\u003C/span>\n\n---\n\n## Research & Exploration\n\n*Early-stage ideas we're thinking about. No timelines yet.*\n\n| Area | Idea | Stage |\n|------|------|-------|\n| **Functions** | Collaborative editing (multiple developers on same function) | Initial research |\n| **Functions** | One-click rollback with visual diff of code changes | User request |\n| **Agents** | Natural language agent configuration | Early prototype |\n| **Registry** | AI-powered function recommendations based on your codebase | Experimenting |\n| **Registry** | Community function templates (pre-built starting points) | Gathering feedback |\n| **Edge** | Edge-native databases (embedded SQLite at the edge) | Exploring |\n| **Billing** | Usage-based pricing with no monthly minimums | Feedback-driven |\n\n---\n\n## How We Prioritize\n\nWe balance several factors when deciding what to build next:\n\n1. **User impact** — How many users benefit, and how much?\n2. **Strategic alignment** — Does it move us toward our long-term vision?\n3. **Technical feasibility** — Can we build it reliably at scale?\n4. **Revenue potential** — Does it help us grow sustainably?\n\nWe gather input from:\n- Direct customer conversations and support tickets\n- Feature requests from the dashboard\n- GitHub issues and discussions\n- Internal product team analysis\n\n---\n\n## Release Philosophy\n\n**Ship when it's ready.** We don't rush features to hit arbitrary dates. We prefer to communicate delays honestly rather than over-promise.\n\n**Semantic versioning.** Breaking changes are rare and communicated well in advance.\n\n**Deprecation policy.** When we retire features, we give at least 90 days notice with migration guidance.\n\n**Changelog.** We document every significant change in our [changelog](https://functionfly.com/changelog/) and [GitHub releases](https://github.com/functionfly/functionfly/releases).\n\n---\n\n## Join the Community\n\nWe're building in the open and want you along for the journey.\n\n[![Discord](https://img.shields.io/discord/123456789?label=Discord)](https://discord.gg/FGnseK9Bp)\n\n- **[Discord Community](https://discord.gg/FGnseK9Bp)** — **Invite-only launch this month!** Join the community to get early access, share feedback, and connect with the team\n- [GitHub Discussions](https://github.com/functionfly/functionfly/discussions) — Share ideas and see what others are asking for\n- [Feedback Form](https://functionfly.com/feedback) — Send private feedback directly to our product team\n\n---\n\n## Status Legend\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-testing\">Testing\u003C/span> | In final QA before release |\n| \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-beta\">Beta\u003C/span> | Available for early access |\n| \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-in-progress\">In Progress\u003C/span> | Actively being built |\n| \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-planned\">Planned\u003C/span> | Scheduled for development |\n| \u003Cspan class=\"badge badge-design\">Design\u003C/span> | Defining specifications |","src/content/docs/roadmap/index.mdx","ec9fb538ca41894b","runtimes/bun",{"id":3202,"data":3204,"body":3210,"filePath":3211,"digest":3212,"rendered":3213},{"title":3205,"description":3206,"editUrl":8,"head":3207,"template":10,"sidebar":3208,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Bun Runtime","Bun runtime environment for FunctionFly functions",[],{"hidden":13,"attrs":3209},{},"FunctionFly's Bun runtime provides a high-performance JavaScript/TypeScript execution environment with native TypeScript support, built-in utilities, and exceptional speed.\n\n## Supported Versions\n\n| Version | Status | Notes |\n|---------|--------|-------|\n| Bun 1.0+ | Supported | Recommended |\n| Bun 1.1 | Supported | Latest |\n\n## Runtime Features\n\nThe Bun runtime provides:\n\n- **Native TypeScript** - No transpilation step needed\n- **Fast cold starts** - Extremely quick initialization\n- **Built-in utilities** - `Bun.serve`, `SQLite`, file system APIs\n- **Web-standard APIs** - Fetch, WebSocket, crypto\n- **Hot reload** - Development mode with instant updates\n\n## Function Structure\n\nA Bun function must export a handler:\n\n```typescript\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request): Promise\u003CResponse> {\n    return Response.json({\n      message: \"Hello from Bun!\"\n    });\n  }\n};\n```\n\n## Request Object\n\nThe `Request` object follows web standards:\n\n```typescript\ninterface Request {\n  method: string;       // GET, POST, etc.\n  headers: Headers;     // HTTP headers\n  url: string;          // Full URL\n  path: string;         // URL path\n  params: URLSearchParams; // Query parameters\n  body: unknown;        // Parsed body (JSON, form, etc.)\n}\n```\n\n## Response Format\n\nReturn a standard `Response`:\n\n```typescript\nreturn Response.json({\n  status: 200,\n  body: { message: \"Hello\" }\n});\n\n// Or with full control\nreturn new Response(JSON.stringify(data), {\n  status: 201,\n  headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\" }\n});\n```\n\n## Example Functions\n\n### HTTP API Handler\n\n```typescript\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request): Promise\u003CResponse> {\n    const url = new URL(request.url);\n    const path = url.pathname;\n\n    if (request.method === \"GET\" && path === \"/users\") {\n      const users = [\n        { id: \"1\", name: \"Alice\", email: \"alice@example.com\" },\n        { id: \"2\", name: \"Bob\", email: \"bob@example.com\" }\n      ];\n      return Response.json({ users });\n    }\n\n    if (request.method === \"POST\" && path === \"/users\") {\n      const body = await request.json();\n      const newUser = {\n        id: crypto.randomUUID(),\n        ...body\n      };\n      return Response.json(newUser, { status: 201 });\n    }\n\n    return Response.json({ error: \"Not found\" }, { status: 404 });\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### Webhook Processor\n\n```typescript\nimport { crypto } from \"crypto\";\n\nconst WEBHOOK_SECRET = process.env.WEBHOOK_SECRET;\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request): Promise\u003CResponse> {\n    const signature = request.headers.get(\"x-signature\") || \"\";\n    const body = await request.text();\n\n    if (!verifySignature(body, signature, WEBHOOK_SECRET || \"\")) {\n      return Response.json({ error: \"Invalid signature\" }, { status: 401 });\n    }\n\n    const event = JSON.parse(body);\n    console.log(\"Webhook received:\", event.type);\n\n    return Response.json({ received: true });\n  }\n};\n\nfunction verifySignature(body: string, signature: string, secret: string): boolean {\n  const expected = crypto\n    .createHmac(\"sha256\", secret)\n    .update(body)\n    .digest(\"hex\");\n\n  return signature === `sha256=${expected}`;\n}\n```\n\n### Data Transformation\n\n```typescript\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request): Promise\u003CResponse> {\n    const body = await request.json();\n\n    const transformed = {\n      id: body.id,\n      name: `${body.first_name} ${body.last_name}`.trim(),\n      email: body.email?.toLowerCase(),\n      timestamp: body.created_at\n    };\n\n    return Response.json(transformed);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n## Bun-Specific Features\n\n### SQLite Database\n\n```typescript\nimport { Database } from \"bun:sqlite\";\n\nconst db = new Database(\":memory:\");\ndb.run(\"CREATE TABLE users (id TEXT, name TEXT)\");\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request): Promise\u003CResponse> {\n    db.run(\"INSERT INTO users VALUES (?, ?)\", [\"1\", \"Alice\"]);\n\n    const users = db.query(\"SELECT * FROM users\").all();\n    return Response.json({ users });\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### File System Access\n\n```typescript\nimport { readFile, writeFile } from \"fs/promises\";\nimport { join } from \"path\";\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(request: Request): Promise\u003CResponse> {\n    const filePath = join(\"/tmp\", \"data.json\");\n\n    if (request.method === \"POST\") {\n      const body = await request.json();\n      await writeFile(filePath, JSON.stringify(body));\n      return Response.json({ saved: true });\n    }\n\n    const data = await readFile(filePath, \"utf-8\");\n    return Response.json(JSON.parse(data));\n  }\n};\n```\n\n### Serving Static Files\n\n```typescript\nimport { fileServer, serve } from \"bun\";\n\nexport default {\n  port: 3000,\n  fetch(request: Request): Response {\n    return fileServer(\"./public\")(request);\n  }\n};\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nAccess via `process.env`:\n\n```typescript\nconst apiKey = process.env.API_KEY;\nconst dbUrl = process.env.DATABASE_URL;\n```\n\n## Timeout and Limits\n\n| Resource | Default | Maximum |\n|----------|---------|---------|\n| Timeout | 30s | 300s (5 min) |\n| Memory | 256 MB | 1024 MB |\n| CPU | 10s | 60s |\n\n## Cold Start\n\nBun has extremely fast cold starts:\n\n- First invocation: ~10-50ms\n- Subsequent invocations: ~1-5ms\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use native TypeScript** - No transpilation needed\n2. **Leverage built-ins** - Bun.serve, SQLite, etc.\n3. **Keep functions stateless** - Between invocations\n4. **Handle errors gracefully** - Return appropriate status codes\n5. **Use `Bun.env` for env vars** - Type-safe access\n6. **Minimize dependencies** - Use built-in APIs when possible","src/content/docs/runtimes/bun.md","5f4e715f771b7a67",{"html":3214,"metadata":3215},"\u003Cp>FunctionFly’s Bun runtime provides a high-performance JavaScript/TypeScript execution environment with native TypeScript support, built-in utilities, and exceptional speed.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"supported-versions\">Supported Versions\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#supported-versions\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Supported Versions”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003Ctable>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Version\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Status\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Notes\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Bun 1.0+\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Supported\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Recommended\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>Bun 1.1\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Supported\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Latest\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"runtime-features\">Runtime Features\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#runtime-features\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Runtime Features”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>The Bun runtime provides:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Native TypeScript\u003C/strong> - No transpilation step needed\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Fast cold starts\u003C/strong> - Extremely quick initialization\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Built-in utilities\u003C/strong> - \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">Bun.serve\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">SQLite\u003C/code>, file system APIs\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Web-standard APIs\u003C/strong> - Fetch, WebSocket, crypto\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Hot reload\u003C/strong> - Development mode with instant updates\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"function-structure\">Function Structure\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#function-structure\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Function Structure”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>A Bun function must export a handler:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"expressive-code\">\u003Clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/_astro/ec.v4551.css\">\u003Cscript type=\"module\" src=\"/_astro/ec.0vx5m.js\">\u003C/script>\u003Cfigure class=\"frame not-content\">\u003Cfigcaption class=\"header\">\u003C/figcaption>\u003Cpre data-language=\"typescript\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#C792EA;--1:#8844AE\">export\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#C792EA;--1:#8844AE\">default\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> {\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan class=\"indent\">  \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#C792EA;--1:#8844AE\">async\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">fetch\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D9F5DD;--1:#111111\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D7DBE0;--1:#403F53\">request\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#7FDBCA;--1:#096E72\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--1:#111111\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#FFCB8B\">Request\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D9F5DD\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#7FDBCA;--1:#096E72\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#FFCB8B;--1:#111111\">Promise\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#FFCB8B;--1:#11111