lue\u003C/code> (String)\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">void\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>KV write\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h3\">\u003Ch3 id=\"classes\">Classes\u003C/h3>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#classes\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Classes”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003Ctable>\u003Cthead>\u003Ctr>\u003Cth>Class\u003C/th>\u003Cth>Description\u003C/th>\u003C/tr>\u003C/thead>\u003Ctbody>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">FunctionFly::Function\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Base class; subclass and implement \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">#handle\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003Ctr>\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">FunctionFly::Context\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\u003Ctd>Execution context (function name, version)\u003C/td>\u003C/tr>\u003C/tbody>\u003C/table>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"limitations\">Limitations\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#limitations\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Limitations”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>mruby only\u003C/strong> — No MRI gems or native extensions\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Single-threaded\u003C/strong> — No concurrency primitives\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Cstrong>Limited stdlib\u003C/strong> — Subset of Ruby standard library\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>",{"headings":4172,"localImagePaths":4198,"remoteImagePaths":4199,"frontmatter":4200,"imagePaths":4201},[4173,4175,4176,4177,4180,4183,4184,4185,4186,4189,4190,4191,4192,4194,4197],{"depth":12,"slug":4174,"text":4161},"ruby-sdk",{"depth":25,"slug":668,"text":669},{"depth":25,"slug":665,"text":666},{"depth":25,"slug":4178,"text":4179},"function-base-class","Function Base Class",{"depth":25,"slug":4181,"text":4182},"module-methods","Module Methods",{"depth":25,"slug":3227,"text":3228},{"depth":61,"slug":3230,"text":3231},{"depth":61,"slug":3233,"text":3234},{"depth":61,"slug":4187,"text":4188},"using-host-functions","Using Host Functions",{"depth":25,"slug":3299,"text":3300},{"depth":25,"slug":641,"text":642},{"depth":25,"slug":2517,"text":2518},{"depth":61,"slug":4193,"text":4182},"module-methods-1",{"depth":61,"slug":4195,"text":4196},"classes","Classes",{"depth":25,"slug":826,"text":827},[],[],{"title":4161,"description":4162},[],"sdks/rust",{"id":4202,"data":4204,"body":4210,"filePath":4211,"digest":4212,"rendered":4213},{"title":4205,"description":4206,"editUrl":8,"head":4207,"template":10,"sidebar":4208,"pagefind":8,"draft":13},"Rust SDK","Rust SDK for building FunctionFly functions",[],{"hidden":13,"attrs":4209},{},"# Rust SDK\n\nThe FunctionFly Rust SDK provides a trait-based API for building FunctionFly functions in Rust, compiled to WebAssembly.\n\n## Installation\n\nAdd to your `Cargo.toml`:\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\nfunctionfly-sdk = \"1.0\"\nserde = { version = \"1.0\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1.0\"\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```rust\nuse functionfly_sdk::{Function, Context};\n\nstruct MyFunction;\n\nimpl Function for MyFunction {\n    fn handle(&self, input: &str, _ctx: &Context) -> Result\u003CString, String> {\n        Ok(r#\"{\"message\": \"Hello from Rust!\"}\"#.to_string())\n    }\n}\n\nfunctionfly_sdk::run!(MyFunction);\n```\n\n## Function Trait\n\nAll functions implement the `Function` trait:\n\n```rust\npub trait Function {\n    /// Process the input and return the output.\n    fn handle(&self, input: &str, ctx: &Context) -> Result\u003CString, String>;\n}\n```\n\n## The `run!` Macro\n\nThe `run!` macro registers the required WASM entry points:\n\n```rust\nfunctionfly_sdk::run!(MyFunction);\n```\n\nThis generates:\n- `init()` — Called once at cold start\n- `execute(ptr, len)` — Main execution entry point\n- `alloc(size)` — Memory allocator\n- `dealloc(ptr, size)` — Memory deallocator\n\n## Host Functions\n\nAccess FunctionFly platform services:\n\n```rust\nuse functionfly_sdk::{log, get_env, kv_get, kv_set, fetch};\n\n// Logging\nlog(\"Processing request\");\n\n// Environment variables\nlet api_key = get_env(\"API_KEY\").unwrap_or_default();\n\n// Key-value store\nkv_set(\"counter\", \"42\");\nlet value = kv_get(\"counter\").unwrap_or_default();\n\n// HTTP fetch\nlet response = fetch(\"https://api.example.com/data\").unwrap_or_default;\n```\n\n## Context\n\nThe `Context` struct provides execution metadata:\n\n```rust\nuse functionfly_sdk::Context;\n\nlet ctx = Context::new();\n// ctx.function_name — Name of the function\n// ctx.version — Deployment version\n```\n\n## Example Functions\n\n### HTTP API Handler\n\n```rust\nuse functionfly_sdk::{Function, Context};\nuse serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\nuse serde_json::json;\n\n#[derive(Deserialize)]\nstruct Request {\n    method: String,\n    body: Option\u003Cserde_json::Value>,\n}\n\n#[derive(Serialize)]\nstruct User {\n    id: String,\n    name: String,\n    email: String,\n}\n\nstruct UserAPI;\n\nimpl Function for UserAPI {\n    fn handle(&self, input: &str, _ctx: &Context) -> Result\u003CString, String> {\n        let request: Request = serde_json::from_str(input)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Invalid JSON: {}\", e))?;\n\n        match request.method.as_str() {\n            \"GET\" => {\n                let users = vec![\n                    User { id: \"1\".into(), name: \"Alice\".into(), email: \"alice@example.com\".into() },\n                    User { id: \"2\".into(), name: \"Bob\".into(), email: \"bob@example.com\".into() },\n                ];\n                Ok(json!({ \"status\": 200, \"body\": { \"users\": users } }).to_string())\n            }\n            \"POST\" => {\n                let body = request.body.unwrap_or_default();\n                let user = User {\n                    id: \"3\".into(),\n                    name: body[\"name\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").into(),\n                    email: body[\"email\"].as_str().unwrap_or(\"\").into(),\n                };\n                Ok(json!({ \"status\": 201, \"body\": user }).to_string())\n            }\n            _ => Ok(r#\"{\"status\": 405, \"body\": {\"error\": \"Method not allowed\"}}\"#.into()),\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfunctionfly_sdk::run!(UserAPI);\n```\n\n### Data Transformation\n\n```rust\nuse functionfly_sdk::{Function, Context};\nuse serde::Deserialize;\n\n#[derive(Deserialize)]\nstruct Input {\n    body: InputBody,\n}\n\n#[derive(Deserialize)]\nstruct InputBody {\n    id: String,\n    first_name: String,\n    last_name: String,\n    email: String,\n    created_at: String,\n}\n\nstruct Transformer;\n\nimpl Function for Transformer {\n    fn handle(&self, input: &str, _ctx: &Context) -> Result\u003CString, String> {\n        let req: Input = serde_json::from_str(input)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Invalid JSON: {}\", e))?;\n\n        let output = serde_json::json!({\n            \"status\": 200,\n            \"body\": {\n                \"id\": req.body.id,\n                \"name\": format!(\"{} {}\", req.body.first_name, req.body.last_name).trim(),\n                \"email\": req.body.email.to_lowercase(),\n                \"timestamp\": req.body.created_at\n            }\n        });\n\n        Ok(output.to_string())\n    }\n}\n\nfunctionfly_sdk::run!(Transformer);\n```\n\n## Building for WASM\n\n```bash\n# Add the WASM target\nrustup target add wasm32-wasip1\n\n# Build\ncargo build --target wasm32-wasip1 --release\n\n# Optimize (optional)\nwasm-opt -O3 target/wasm32-wasip1/release/my-function.wasm -o optimized.wasm\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\nReturn `Result\u003CString, String>` from `handle`:\n\n```rust\nimpl Function for SafeFunction {\n    fn handle(&self, input: &str, ctx: &Context) -> Result\u003CString, String> {\n        let request: serde_json::Value = serde_json::from_str(input)\n            .map_err(|e| format!(\"Invalid JSON: {}\", e))?;\n\n        let result = process(&request)?;\n        Ok(serde_json::json!({ \"status\": 200, \"body\": result }).to_string())\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## API Reference\n\n### Traits\n\n| Trait | Method | Signature |\n|-------|--------|-----------|\n| `Function` | `handle` | `fn handle(&self, input: &str, ctx: &Context) -> Result\u003CString, String>` |\n\n### Host Functions\n\n| Function | Signature | Description |\n|----------|-----------|-------------|\n| `log` | `fn log(msg: &str)` | Log a message |\n| `get_env` | `fn get_env(key: &str) -> Option\u003CString>` | Get environment variable |\n| `kv_get` | `fn kv_get(key: &str) -> Option\u003CString>` | Read from KV store |\n| `kv_set` | `fn kv_set(key: &str, value: &str)` | Write to KV store |\n| `fetch` | `fn fetch(url: &str) -> Option\u003CString>` | HTTP fetch |\n\n### Macros\n\n| Macro | Usage | Description |\n|-------|-------|-------------|\n| `run!` | `functionfly_sdk::run!(MyFunction)` | Register WASM entry points |","src/content/docs/sdks/rust.md","9597d6ebefef2f3b",{"html":4214,"metadata":4215},"\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h1\">\u003Ch1 id=\"rust-sdk\">Rust SDK\u003C/h1>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#rust-sdk\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\">Section titled “Rust SDK”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>The FunctionFly Rust SDK provides a trait-based API for building FunctionFly functions in Rust, compiled to WebAssembly.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"installation\">Installation\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#installation\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\u003Cpath fill=\"currentcolor\" d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.